<Article
  title="Funds accounting"
  description="Gross source value, collector receipts, consolidation holdings and fees for the transaction sets attributed to the COLDCARD incident."
  standfirst="The published totals describe different transaction sets and different stages of the same flows. This page separates them and labels every attribution."
  depth="plain"
  kicker="Evidence"
>
  <Answer>
  <p>
    The principal BTC figures measure four different things: value consumed from
    source addresses, value received by first collectors, value retained after
    consolidation, and transaction fees. They also depend on whether the set is
    limited to 500 transactions or includes 695 more transactions that
    <a href="/record/sources/clay-earlier-waves-thread/">Block preliminarily associated by a shared fingerprint</a>
    and <a href="https://x.com/glxyresearch/status/2083181683067506899" rel="noopener nofollow">Galaxy Research attribute to the same operator</a>.
    Keeping the stage and the set attached to each number removes most of the
    apparent disagreement.
  </p>
  </Answer>

  <div class="kpi-row">
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--i:0">
      <div class="kpi-card__value" style="color:var(--red)"><span>594.51379184</span><sup>BTC</sup></div>
      <div class="kpi-card__label">500-transaction set, gross</div>
      <div class="kpi-card__note">Value consumed from 500 source addresses in blocks 960,188 to 960,191. The first collector received 594.47722484 BTC after {fig('sweptFeesBtc')} in fees.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--i:1">
      <div class="kpi-card__value" style="color:var(--red)"><span>1,082.65</span><sup>BTC</sup></div>
      <div class="kpi-card__label">Galaxy's published gross total</div>
      <div class="kpi-card__note">Galaxy attributes the 500-transaction set and 695 additional transactions to one operator. This site's reconciliation of the pinned chain-derived dataset gives {fig('totalGrossBtc')} gross if that attribution is accepted.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--i:2">
      <div class="kpi-card__value"><span>1,195</span></div>
      <div class="kpi-card__label">Original source addresses re-derived</div>
      <div class="kpi-card__note">Galaxy publishes 1,196. This site's own count reaches 1,196 by adding one first collector that later spends, but Galaxy has not published its counting method.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--i:3">
      <div class="kpi-card__value" style="color:var(--amber)"><span>1,082.56919591</span><sup>BTC</sup></div>
      <div class="kpi-card__label">Theft-linked after consolidation</div>
      <div class="kpi-card__note">The amount attributable to the two sets in four final holdings. Later unsolicited deposits are excluded. No funds left the four-address cluster after final consolidation by the stated check time.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="cap">
    Transaction-set figures are fixed to the pinned chain-derived dataset at
    commit <code>47d8f554</code>. The four-address balance check is fixed to
    Bitcoin block 960,525 at 06:48 UTC on 1 August 2026. Neither figure tracks
    live balances. The cards measure the 30 July transaction sets this
    page reconciles and nothing wider. Galaxy Research has since published a
    larger estimated total covering a third wave that is not reconciled here;
    it is kept <a href="#galaxy-revision">separate below</a> rather than folded
    into these figures.
  </p>

  <p>
    If your own addresses may be affected, start with the
    <a href="/risk/">risk assessment</a>, which works from the firmware a seed
    was generated on.
  </p>

  <h2>What the principal figures measure</h2>

  <p>
    The narrower set contains 500 transactions spending 1,324 UTXOs from 500
    distinct source addresses. The transactions confirmed in four consecutive
    blocks, 960,188 to 960,191. Their inputs total 594.51379184 BTC, of which
    594.47722484 BTC reached one first collector and {fig('sweptFeesBtc')} was paid in
    transaction fees. TFTC publishes the collector receipt, not the gross input
    value.
    <Claim
      basis="derived"
      scope="This site's calculation of the 500-transaction set's counts, block range, gross input, collector receipt and fees"
      source="Privacy-safe integer-satoshi recheck of the pinned Kelbie chain dataset, with TFTC's collector receipt retained as the published comparison"
      href="/record/evidence/funds-accounting-47d8f554-20260801T064817Z.json"
    />
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="https://x.com/Rob1Ham/status/2082896614218203616" rel="noopener nofollow">Rob Hamilton's preliminary post</a>
    reported the same 1,324 UTXOs, 500 transactions and approximately 594.48 BTC,
    followed by a consolidation of about 562 BTC. It described a "3 block
    window", while the transactions are confirmed across four blocks. The block
    timestamps run from 01:36:08 to 01:51:26 UTC, a span of 15 minutes 18
    seconds, consistent with Hamilton's separate description of an approximately
    15-minute period.
    <Claim
      basis="reported"
      scope="Hamilton's published preliminary figures"
      source="Rob Hamilton primary post, captured 1 Aug 2026"
      href="/record/sources/robhamilton-preliminary-sweep/"
    />
  </p>

  <p>
    The first collector later spent 341 outputs into the largest final holding
    while retaining a remainder. The 695-transaction set followed a separate
    path through three first collectors and two batch consolidations. A single
    first collector and four final holdings are therefore successive stages of
    the flows, not competing descriptions of one stage.
  </p>

  <Disclosure id="galaxy-attribution" title="Galaxy's wider attribution" note="1,196 addresses, 1,082.65 BTC, one attributed operator" open>

  <p>
    <a href="https://x.com/glxyresearch/status/2083181683067506899" rel="noopener nofollow">Galaxy Research reported 1,196 addresses and {fig('galaxyGrossBtc')}</a>
    from 01:10:20 to 01:51:26 UTC on 30 July, across blocks 960,183 to 960,191.
    It attributed the wider set to one operator using the transaction pattern
    identified by Block. Galaxy also published a derivation-path count of 1,183
    BIP-84, 7 BIP-49 and 6 BIP-44 addresses.
    <Claim
      basis="reported"
      scope="Galaxy's published address count, gross BTC total, time window, derivation-path counts and transaction-pattern description"
      source="Galaxy Research primary post, captured 1 Aug 2026"
      href="/record/sources/glxyresearch-flow-map/"
    />
  </p>

  <blockquote>
    Galaxy described the repeated target as a "hardcoded 30.0 sat/vB" fee rate
    with no change output.
    <cite><a href="https://x.com/glxyresearch/status/2083181683067506899" rel="noopener nofollow">Galaxy Research, X, 31 Jul 2026</a></cite>
  </blockquote>

  <p>
    Realised fee rates cluster near that target but vary slightly because fees
    are whole satoshis. Across the source and consolidation transactions, the
    fee total in this site's reconciliation of the pinned chain-derived
    dataset is {fig('totalFeesBtc')}.
    <Claim
      basis="derived"
      scope="This site's 0.08399331 BTC aggregate fee calculation for the attributed source and consolidation transactions"
      source="Privacy-safe integer-satoshi accounting of 1,195 source transactions and three consolidations in the pinned Kelbie dataset"
      href="/record/evidence/funds-accounting-47d8f554-20260801T064817Z.json"
    />
    That is the total paid to miners, not a measure of overpayment. Galaxy's
    comparison with prevailing fee rates is a separate reported estimate.
  </p>

  <p>
    In this site's check, the source transactions from the two sets spend
    from 1,195 original addresses: 1,182 native SegWit P2WPKH, 7 P2SH and 6
    legacy P2PKH. Adding the native SegWit first collector when it later spends
    produces Galaxy's 1,196 total and numerically matches its reported 1,183
    BIP-84, 7 BIP-49 and 6 BIP-44 counts. This is a plausible reconciliation,
    not a verified description of Galaxy's method. On-chain output types do not
    independently reveal wallet derivation paths, and the post does not define
    whether an internal collector is included in its address count.
    <Claim
      basis="derived"
      scope="The reconciliation between 1,195 original source addresses and Galaxy's published count of 1,196"
      source="Output-type and address-role re-derivation from the attributed transaction sets; derivation paths remain Galaxy's reported classification"
      href="/record/evidence/funds-accounting-47d8f554-20260801T064817Z.json"
    />
  </p>

  <div class="mermaid-wrap">
