  <p>
    The US$38 million and US$70 million figures primarily reflect different BTC
    sets, 594.48 BTC versus about 1,082.6 BTC, as well as each publisher's BTC/USD
    conversion time. Galaxy's approximately US$88.6m belongs to a third set
    again, the three-wave scope described above. The later 45.9 BTC cluster is
    not included in the main accounting on this page because its relationship to
    the principal set has not been established. Tracker rows carry the figure
    held at the stated capture time; those sites publish live totals that have
    continued to move since.
  </p>

  <p>
    The two newest rows are wider again than anything reconciled on this page.
    Kelbie's 2 August tracker total of {fig('kelbieTrackerBtc')} across
    {fig('kelbieTrackerAddresses')} is numerically close to Galaxy's revised
    1,367.05 BTC across 4,585 addresses, but neither source states that the two
    sets are the same, and the tracker post does not itemise which waves its
    set counts, so the rows are kept separate rather than read as one
    measurement.
    <Claim
      basis="reported"
      scope="Kelbie's tracker total of 1,367 BTC across 4,620 drained addresses, its victim-to-current-position method and its timeline claim"
