  <Disclosure id="set-500" title="What the 500-address set shows">

  <p>
    Within the 500-source-address set, gross amounts consumed range from
    0.14999770 BTC to {fig('lossLargest')}, with a median of {fig('lossMedian')}. Because
    the set has an even 500 values, that median is the average of its two middle
    values and can fall on a half-satoshi; it is a statistical summary, not an
    on-chain amount. Of those addresses, 110 held more than 1 BTC and another 16
    held exactly 1 BTC. The observed minimum is {fig('lossFloor')}; the data
    do not establish that it was an operator-selected threshold.
    <Claim
      basis="derived"
      scope="The minimum, median and one-BTC distribution figures for the 500-address set"
      source="Privacy-safe wave-3 distribution in the public funds-accounting artefact; address-level inputs are withheld"
      href="/record/evidence/funds-accounting-47d8f554-20260801T064817Z.json"
    />
  </p>

  <p>
    Hamilton reported that all addresses in the 500-transaction set used
    single-signature spending conditions, none used Taproot, and the spent UTXOs
    dated from 2021 to 2026. Those are properties of the observed outputs and
    spending scripts, not proof of each owner's wallet configuration or seed
    creation date. The pinned chain dataset reports output classifications for
    the original source addresses: 1,182 native SegWit P2WPKH, 7 P2SH and 6
    legacy P2PKH across both attributed sets. These counts numerically reconcile with
    Galaxy's published BIP-84, BIP-49 and BIP-44 figures as described above,
    without independently establishing those derivation paths.
    <Claim
      basis="reported"
      captured="1 Aug 2026"
      scope="Hamilton's output-type observations and Galaxy's published derivation-path counts"
      source="Rob Hamilton and Galaxy Research primary posts; the output-type counts are classifications reported by the pinned chain dataset, not measurements made here"
      href="/record/sources/robhamilton-preliminary-sweep/"
    />
  </p>

  </Disclosure>

